mindmap
  root(("C Strings"))
    String_Fundamentals
      Null-terminated char arrays
      Last char is always backslash-zero
      String_literals
        Stored in read-only dot-rodata
        char-star s points to literal
      Char_arrays
        char s array mutable local copy
        sizeof includes null terminator
      strlen returns length excluding null
    string_h_Library
      strlen function
        Counts chars before null
        O-n linear scan
      strcpy and strncpy
        strcpy dangerous no bounds check
        strncpy safer with size limit
      strcat and strncat
        Concatenates strings together
        strncat checks remaining space
      strcmp and strncmp
        Returns 0 if strings equal
        Lexicographic ASCII comparison
      strstr function
        Substring search
        Returns pointer to first match
      strchr and strrchr
        Find first or last char
        Returns pointer or NULL
      strtok function
        Tokenizes string by delimiters
        Modifies input not reentrant
        Use strtok_r for reentrant
    String_IO
      printf and puts
        Percent-s format specifier
        puts adds newline automatically
      scanf percent-s
        Reads until whitespace
        Always specify field width
      fgets safe line input
        Includes newline in buffer
        Remove with strchr or strcspn
    Character_Processing
      ctype_h functions
        isupper islower isdigit
        isalpha isspace ispunct
      Loop over chars until null
    Array_of_Strings
      2D char array fixed width
      Pointer array variable length
    Common_Mistakes
      Buffer overflow with strcpy
      Missing null terminator
      Confusing char vs string literal
